# Security headers for every response (Cloudflare Pages reads this file; it is not served).
# Content-Security-Policy (pages only): only this site, Supabase, Open-Meteo and Zippopotam may be contacted; no inline scripts
# (theme.js and swreg.js replace them). 'wasm-unsafe-eval' lets the on-phone cut-out model run.
# It is set on the HTML pages only: the cut-out worker (vendor/bgworker.mjs) needs eval, which the policy forbids,
# and a worker gets its policy from its own response, so it is left without one. Pages are the attack surface.
# HSTS: browsers already force HTTPS for every .app domain (HSTS preload list); the header makes it explicit.
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin: Cloudflare adds "*" by default; removed, since no other site needs to read these files.
# Adding a new outside service (an API, CDN or image host) means adding its address here, or the app will block it.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), geolocation=(self), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  ! Access-Control-Allow-Origin

